[628.915803, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2m\u001b[H\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2;91H\u001b[1K\u001b[34m\r\n\u2192 Entering PlanSync Coding Mode (task: cmqckbxz401gp7qsgl9kacfvs, run: cmqckhn1v01ih7qsgeg7\u001b[39m\u001b[4;91H\u001b[1K\u001b[34m\rbki1h, executor: alice)\u001b[39m\u001b[5;91H\u001b[1K\r\nHere is my approach for this research task before proceeding:\u001b[30X\u001b[7;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r---\u001b[9;91H\u001b[1K\r\n**Task:** Review pay/card-form spec \u2014 validate the `CardForm` component design against the \u001b[11;91H\u001b[1K\rplan\u001b[12;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r**Deliverable identified:**\u001b[14;91H\u001b[1K\r- Slug: `pay/card-form`\u001b[15;91H\u001b[1K\r- Title: \u652f\u4ed8\u5361\u7247\u8868\u5355\u7ec4\u4ef6\u001b[16;91H\u001b[1K\r- Body: `CardForm.tsx \u4fe1\u7528\u5361\u8f93\u5165\u7ec4\u4ef6`\r\n- Maps to: `src/components/pay/CardForm.*` (file_glob)\u001b[37X\u001b[18;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r**Review approach:**\u001b[20;91H\u001b[1K\r\n1. **Check file existence** \u2014 look for `src/components/pay/CardForm.*` in the repo to see i\u001b[22;91H\u001b[1K\rf any implementation already exists\r\n2. **Validate spec completeness** \u2014 assess whether the deliverable spec is sufficient: does\r\n it capture field requirements (card number, expiry, CVV, cardholder name), validation rule\u001b[25;91H\u001b[1K\rs, and tokenization strategy?\r\n3. **Check PCI DSS alignment** \u2014 verify the design does not store raw card numbers (constra\r\nint from the plan); review whether a tokenization/iframe/third-party approach is specified \u001b[28;91H\u001b[1K\ror needed\r\n4. **Check TypeScript & test standards** \u2014 confirm the spec implies strict-mode TS and that\r\n the component design is testable at >80% coverage\u001b[41X\r\n5. **Document findings** \u2014 post a `plansync_comment_create` with the review results and any\u001b[32;91H\u001b[1K\r recommendations or open questions\u001b[33;91H\u001b[1K\r\nNo code will be written \u2014 this is a pure review/research output delivered as a PlanSync com\u001b[35;91H\u001b[1K\rment.\u001b[36;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r---\u001b[38;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\rShall I proceed with this approach?\u001b[40;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[34m\r\u2190 Returned to PlanSync Terminal\u001b[39m\u001b[42;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[70C"]
